#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "79841c0d-e191-566b-8fe2-63828dcfc23a" :question/math-academy-id "e-4439" :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059485 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/id #uuid "51f60726-3d12-507e-b942-5d316fc28bd0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4440" :question/problem "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059486 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/id #uuid "afd06762-0a78-5559-b035-98bd05e6c084" :question/math-academy-id "e-4441" :question/problem "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276677 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "beed0687-2ccd-5451-9b6e-1c9d14f2afed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276679} {:answer/id #uuid "9c79abcb-ee2a-52c0-a655-2eb3b3298fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276680} {:answer/id #uuid "ed3dd8dd-9bcf-5d78-8296-626c52cc9433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276681} {:answer/id #uuid "c225dd50-8746-5bc3-b0e3-3dd591ccbab8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276682} {:answer/id #uuid "84521bb6-d919-5947-9e7c-4b07a209f74d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84521bb6-d919-5947-9e7c-4b07a209f74d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276683} :answer-field/id #uuid "93d591c2-000d-5aae-9b6c-7936672e8053" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276678}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "845a8110-db5a-5eb7-8c6a-c2552c5f87a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-1092" :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry ${b}_{22}$ in the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 13 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${b}_{22}=7$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $7$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & ∗ & -6 \\\\ ∗ & 7 & ∗ \\\\ 5 & ∗ & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=7$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 4-(-6)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =12-(-30) \\\\  & =42.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059911 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c0a4da-b48c-57f2-8331-f599d27a61ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-r - 5rt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056186} {:answer/id #uuid "151ec30f-0156-58b5-b5ae-8bd06ff80ea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-r^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056187} {:answer/id #uuid "26b9af6a-74f1-5cf0-9e37-e7285876a3e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056188} {:answer/id #uuid "292a37f8-50f6-5675-bca0-8ebaa9dcbf4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4r^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056189} {:answer/id #uuid "6c561c2c-0c10-5e3a-afb2-8c5ce5d0cce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3rs + 2rt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c561c2c-0c10-5e3a-afb2-8c5ce5d0cce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3rs + 2rt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056190} :answer-field/id #uuid "37846d32-b064-507f-be21-ccc91075858f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47a0f2fd-6622-508d-a61d-a108ebab293f" :question/math-academy-id "q-1099" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${d}_{32}$ in the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3s & -{r}^{2} & 2t \\\\ -r & 0 & r \\\\ 5t & 4r & 1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and second column:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3s & ∗ & 2t \\\\ -r & ∗ & r \\\\ ∗ & 4r & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}3s & 2t \\\\ -r & r\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}3s & 2t \\\\ -r & r\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3s\\cdot r-2t\\cdot (-r) \\\\  & =3rs-(-2rt) \\\\  & =3rs+2rt\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cf23f1a-a86d-5d67-8724-0c726f29d882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "285" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276686} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fd8db9-cf95-5c5f-8748-b0457c95f024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "345" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276687} {:answer/id #uuid "03f18565-c276-541e-9226-7739dafbdb7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276688} {:answer/id #uuid "cb40e938-139b-5699-a4f0-0a85fb45bd55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "225" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276689} {:answer/id #uuid "7cfd355a-8f04-586d-a6e7-bf3a4159a391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cfd355a-8f04-586d-a6e7-bf3a4159a391" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "250" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276690} :answer-field/id #uuid "52ee73cf-0a40-530d-bb91-a78969adc594" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b3206426-7895-57dc-9e71-57b7a358da08" :question/math-academy-id "q-127698" :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry ${d}_{23}$ in the matrix\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -12 & 44 & -33 \\\\ 25 & 30 & 41\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${d}_{23}=-33$ (second row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-33$ are removed: \n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & -33 \\\\ 25 & 30 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${d}_{23}=-33$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 25 & 30\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}10 & 2 \\\\ 25 & 30\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =10\\cdot 30-2\\cdot 25 \\\\  & =300-50 \\\\  & =250.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cca4795-f42d-55c8-a9c7-5384cc03c78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf+5f" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276693} {:answer/id #uuid "5fd0c10a-c26c-572b-9a05-84069587b78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{2}+{g}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276694} {:answer/id #uuid "40934120-ed89-554b-91fb-88b74a122a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf(f-g)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276695} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4c8859-ccc8-5842-89ec-80805b18e974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf(f+g)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276696} {:answer/id #uuid "970311e3-4e14-55b5-93f4-ec2948735196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf-3g" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40934120-ed89-554b-91fb-88b74a122a0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "gf(f-g)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276695} :answer-field/id #uuid "37bbeca6-2643-5edd-a7b9-5e2edf1c9dc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "79af0c62-6c1b-55d6-8154-076e57601d0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-128030" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${m}_{31}$ in the matrix\n$M=[\\begin{aligned}-50 & g & f \\\\ f & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & g & -5\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & g & f \\\\ ∗ & {g}^{2} & {f}^{2} \\\\ 20g & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}g & f \\\\ {g}^{2} & {f}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =g\\cdot {f}^{2}-f\\cdot {g}^{2} \\\\  & =g{f}^{2}-f{g}^{2} \\\\  & =gf(f-g)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6613d62-ff37-5db0-b287-427d552fccc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276700} {:answer/id #uuid "2ec2ff13-3b71-5645-8344-533c2e67bb79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276701} {:answer/id #uuid "b08b34de-9a83-521b-96cd-e14b4fe1fe8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276702} {:answer/id #uuid "643f18dc-45b9-58f9-be1a-370f3d299182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276703} {:answer/id #uuid "2df15760-cfbe-5b05-8675-bbb5e9d1f098" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "643f18dc-45b9-58f9-be1a-370f3d299182" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276703} :answer-field/id #uuid "718c722d-df3f-5a39-8b33-e5316583da63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276699}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2fbd8d6-fa74-5a2e-bdd4-9ee7fbfe94f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-18240" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 9 & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & -5 \\\\ ∗ & 11 & x \\\\ 7 & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${d}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot x-11\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =x+55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${d}_{31}$ is $43$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+55 & =43 \\\\ x & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3533297a-1039-56a0-b0cc-22dc1b6c0056" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10+z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276707} {:answer/id #uuid "51178909-aa0b-5954-8261-958a2c91b4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276708}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51178909-aa0b-5954-8261-958a2c91b4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276708} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf6a41e9-50ac-558f-a56d-814d22a0cce6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276706}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "03e055b5-d0f8-53f2-9e9e-d73f97dbbc13" :question/math-academy-id "q-275501" :question/problem "For the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 & y \\\\ 2 & x & z \\\\ 1 & w & 5\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the element ${a}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{12},$ we remove the first row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 3 & ∗ \\\\ 2 & ∗ & z \\\\ 1 & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{12}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & z \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-z\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =10-z\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36c26cc0-0dac-5a9a-90be-3318447ef9e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276711} {:answer/id #uuid "f1ca767d-b19c-5193-9532-f4a99bc4b26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1ca767d-b19c-5193-9532-f4a99bc4b26b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276712} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead1b973-ab23-513f-b921-b750a8990a1a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "18074bc1-0ac7-5c79-ba98-6b0d1083f938" :question/math-academy-id "q-275502" :question/problem "$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is $18$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${c}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${c}_{32}$ is $18$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =18 \\\\ 6x & =30 \\\\ x & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276713 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3739d46d-02d9-52d2-a43c-66905d92a3b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276715} {:answer/id #uuid "65a64608-b3d9-5990-96f5-373a317ec442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276716}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "65a64608-b3d9-5990-96f5-373a317ec442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276716} :answer-field/id #uuid "73d40608-5717-5dd1-9732-d77ac06d67e5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276714}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12b90c27-f9b6-5491-8e56-f08735a304f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-319108" :question/problem "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{22}$ of the entry ${b}_{22}.$\n\n${M}_{22}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $0$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{22} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =6-(-21) \\\\  & =6+21 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb2ee60-64cf-51b0-a6af-56bc76d2af14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276719}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbb2ee60-64cf-51b0-a6af-56bc76d2af14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276719} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef9a26f0-c0a2-5efa-9f1d-fad25349c34c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276718}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f9c853e-7fa9-5b18-a1e7-f539794d4106" :question/math-academy-id "q-319110" :question/problem "For the matrix\n$Y=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{32}$ of the entry ${y}_{32}.$\n\n${M}_{32}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ (third row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ ∗ & -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{32} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-15 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276720 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e1b4442-eca7-5283-9d5d-5bcbd1d67975" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Integer Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "314415fe-7cd9-52b3-80ba-cb0a22a689ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "314415fe-7cd9-52b3-80ba-cb0a22a689ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276722} :answer-field/id #uuid "64537d78-b188-5768-9579-25652dc3ba52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f10c0b88-4a8e-58c9-9d15-7c8f967e4b7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-319112" :question/problem "For the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${c}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d040552-271b-560e-a9ef-d46c351a354f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d040552-271b-560e-a9ef-d46c351a354f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276725} :answer-field/id #uuid "716ee75c-548b-593d-8812-b8ba0789037a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276724}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d45b8ed-5634-5d58-870a-718c8f538e7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-319129" :question/problem "$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $y$ in the matrix above.\n\n$y=$\n {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & ∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-2 & =10 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21f85eeb-27c5-5051-8009-9431ecd18780" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276728} {:answer/id #uuid "eda888d0-7bf8-58da-b004-4c3c684660a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda888d0-7bf8-58da-b004-4c3c684660a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276729} :answer-field/id #uuid "89eaea32-a181-5ab1-8c11-39aca8439e79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05640802-8be2-5778-9f76-e0c423c8b4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05640802-8be2-5778-9f76-e0c423c8b4ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276731} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb235530-ad1e-5380-90e1-31a2ae117c83" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b4e0bf0c-7585-5f5b-934d-8a0791dbf0c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-319146" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 7 \\\\ 6 & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 7 \\\\ ∗ & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa65a73-e750-5052-9249-7c096297ae51" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Value of a Minor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070a7cda-fe29-5b98-9200-9aba9862c0f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=3$ and $k=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276734} {:answer/id #uuid "62951165-341a-54bc-a355-1e24fea0c1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-3$ and $k=6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276735} {:answer/id #uuid "0297a401-f27a-5e46-b31e-41425ff749ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=3$ and $k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276736} {:answer/id #uuid "3da00856-081f-573e-b917-2dc505021757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276737} {:answer/id #uuid "665cf5ac-10dc-5b08-b1e1-50ed7f8f6ce9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=8$ and $k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276738}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0297a401-f27a-5e46-b31e-41425ff749ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$k=3$ and $k=-6$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276736} :answer-field/id #uuid "a849424b-369c-5569-8573-69570a2abc1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7d3c4b09-0a4b-5edb-9bbd-4cd83aed736b" :question/math-academy-id "q-42614" :question/problem "Given that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 9k-15 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ & 1 \\\\ ∗ & -4 & ∗ \\\\ 9k-15 & ∗ & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${m}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 9k-15 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-3)-(9k-15)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-6-(9k-15) \\\\  & =-9k+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${m}_{22}$ is $3{k}^{2}-45$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9k+9 & =3{k}^{2}-45 \\\\ -3k+3 & ={k}^{2}-15 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k-18 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=3$ and $k=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cd72394-b125-540d-80c4-6d8e8ed61845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{q}^{2}p" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276741} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1fde77-77ac-535f-8692-b976c424b4bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{q}^{2}{p}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276742} {:answer/id #uuid "42aeb26b-7d1f-5842-87d7-1aacf7f9ba19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{p}^{2}-3q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276743} {:answer/id #uuid "e9f279b7-f9a3-5932-8ea6-0235acde5c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5pq" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276744} {:answer/id #uuid "56cf3a4e-c942-5bb6-a759-4998e695c68f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6pq" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9f279b7-f9a3-5932-8ea6-0235acde5c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5pq" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276744} :answer-field/id #uuid "3426c01c-ee4c-54ca-aad8-b05d3dc8c72e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276740}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "83b33ace-dbbf-5ce4-ae5e-36a23887dffc" :question/math-academy-id "q-69739" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${e}_{32}$ in the matrix\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}2p & p & -q \\\\ -p & {q}^{2} & 3q \\\\ q & 0 & q\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and the second column:\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}2p & ∗ & -q \\\\ -p & ∗ & 3q \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}2p & -q \\\\ -p & 3q\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2p & -q \\\\ -p & 3q\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2p\\cdot 3q-(-q)\\cdot (-p) \\\\  & =6pq-pq \\\\  & =5pq\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186276746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff88785-9281-5431-86d8-95fd89866787" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Minor in a 3x3 Matrix With Variable Entries"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb9fe303-788d-5158-9a70-2cf60139edda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}-2{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276748} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0615c-e008-5893-b3f5-66480db07b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276749} {:answer/id #uuid "06ee0f7e-4c6c-592a-957e-e0a446147590" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276750} {:answer/id #uuid "cd4de354-b3de-5812-8d84-64885db8bc7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276751} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b1d660-3595-55a5-95a2-11f7cd546d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bb0615c-e008-5893-b3f5-66480db07b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276749} :answer-field/id #uuid "162724ee-f180-51e9-9c63-4ab63212c96a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276747}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b34c44d7-ca23-51bd-b337-4479b87f5ce2" :question/math-academy-id "q-69760" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${t}_{33}$ in the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}y-x & x & {y}^{2} \\\\ -x & y+x & 1 \\\\ {x}^{2} & {y}^{2} & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}y-x & x & ∗ \\\\ -x & y+x & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & {x}^{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}y-x & x \\\\ -x & y+x\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}y-x & x \\\\ -x & y+x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(y-x)\\cdot (y+x)-x\\cdot (-x) \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-{x}^{2}+{x}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}^{2}}+\\cancel{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
